<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Hadoop on Coinidea's Blog</title><link>https://blog.coinidea.com/en/tags/hadoop/</link><description>Recent content in Hadoop on Coinidea's Blog</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Mon, 28 Sep 2015 14:50:42 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://blog.coinidea.com/en/tags/hadoop/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>[Hadoop] Setting Up the CDH Environment</title><link>https://blog.coinidea.com/en/p/hadoop-setting-up-the-cdh-environment/</link><pubDate>Mon, 28 Sep 2015 14:50:42 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.coinidea.com/en/p/hadoop-setting-up-the-cdh-environment/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="1-connect-server"&gt;1. Connect server
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;Use CRT or Xshell to connect to the server remotely.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1 id="2-network-config"&gt;2. Network config
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;h2 id="first-configure-dns-for-the-server-and-check-whether-it-can-access-the-internet"&gt;First, configure DNS for the server and check whether it can access the internet.
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Enter the following command:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;
&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-shell" data-lang="shell"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;ping &lt;span class="o"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;www.baidu.com&lt;span class="o"&gt;][&lt;/span&gt;1&lt;span class="o"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;If you receive a reply from [www.baidu.com][1], it means the server can access the internet. If you get &amp;ldquo;unknown host,&amp;rdquo; the DNS configuration is incorrect and needs to be set up.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;There are two ways to configure DNS:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Temporary solution: edit the resolv.conf file and add &amp;ldquo;nameserver 8.8.8.8&amp;rdquo;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;
&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-shell" data-lang="shell"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;vi /etc/resolv.conf
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;nameserver 8.8.8.8
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Permanent solution: edit the ifcfg_eth0 file and add &amp;ldquo;DNS1=8.8.8.8&amp;rdquo;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;
&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-shell" data-lang="shell"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;vi /etc/sysconfig/network-scripts/ifcfg-eth0
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;DNS1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;8.8.8.8
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;After configuration, run the command &amp;ldquo;service network restart&amp;rdquo;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The second approach is recommended, as the first one will be lost when the server restarts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Disable the firewall&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Enter the command:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;
&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-shell" data-lang="shell"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;service iptables stop
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h1 id="3-file-transfer"&gt;3. File transfer
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;During the installation process, &lt;strong&gt;you may need to upload local files to the server&lt;/strong&gt;. Here is one approach.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Enter the command:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;
&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-shell" data-lang="shell"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;sudo yum install lrzsz
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;After installing the lrzsz package, enter:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;
&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-shell" data-lang="shell"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;rz
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Then select the file you want to upload.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Yum (Yellow dog Updater Modified) is an RPM-based package manager that can automatically download and install RPM packages from specified servers, handling dependency relationships automatically and installing all dependent packages at once, eliminating the tedious process of downloading and installing them one by one.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1 id="4-install-cdh"&gt;4. Install CDH
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;HDFS&lt;/strong&gt;: A distributed file storage system, the open-source Java implementation of GFS.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="http://blog.coinidea.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/09/image0011.jpg"
loading="lazy"
alt="image001"
&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MapReduce&lt;/strong&gt;: A parallel computing programming model for large-scale datasets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="http://blog.coinidea.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/09/image0021.jpg"
loading="lazy"
alt="image002"
&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;HBase: NoSQL column database&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hive: Data warehouse&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zookeeper: Distributed lock service&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pig: Big data analysis platform interface&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Home link: &lt;a class="link" href="http://www.cloudera.com/content/cloudera/en/products-and-services/cdh.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
&gt;http://www.cloudera.com/content/cloudera/en/products-and-services/cdh.html&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Setup:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1. Java&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CentOS 6.7 comes with JDK 1.7, so this step can be skipped. Any JDK-related steps during installation can be ignored.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2. Cloudera Manager Server&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cloudera Manager makes it easy to &lt;strong&gt;manage Hadoop deployments of any scale in production&lt;/strong&gt;. Quickly deploy, configure, and monitor your cluster through an intuitive UI – complete with rolling upgrades, backup and disaster recovery, and customizable alerting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Download:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class="link" href="http://www.cloudera.com/content/cloudera/en/downloads/cloudera_manager/cm-5-4-7.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
&gt;http://www.cloudera.com/content/cloudera/en/downloads/cloudera_manager/cm-5-4-7.html&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Download the latest version 5.4.7.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;After downloading, you will get a file of about 503KB named cloudera-manager-installer.bin. Upload this file (using &amp;ldquo;rz&amp;rdquo;) to a designated folder on the server.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Close selinux:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;
&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-shell" data-lang="shell"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;/etc/selinux/config
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;selinux&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;disabled
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hostname&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You need to modify the hostname of the machine. To check the current hostname, simply type hostname.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Enter:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;
&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-shell" data-lang="shell"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;vi /etc/hosts
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Edit the file and add the line &amp;ldquo;192.168._._ master.com master&amp;rdquo;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Note: when adding datanode nodes, do not name them &amp;ldquo;master&amp;rdquo; &amp;ndash; use names like &amp;ldquo;datanode1&amp;rdquo; instead.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Run the &amp;ldquo;reboot&amp;rdquo; command to restart the server.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3. CDH&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Using cloudera manager&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Navigate to the directory containing cloudera-manager-installer.bin and run:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;
&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-shell" data-lang="shell"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;chmod u+x cloudera-manager-installer.bin
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;./ cloudera-manager-installer.bin
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Keep clicking next. The selected items will be highlighted in bold.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This may take a while, so please be patient&amp;hellip;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Choose express free version.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="http://blog.coinidea.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/09/image0031.png"
loading="lazy"
alt="image003"
&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Display the packages to be installed&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="http://blog.coinidea.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/09/image004.png"
loading="lazy"
alt="image004"
&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Specify CDH cluster hosts&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="http://blog.coinidea.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/09/image005.png"
loading="lazy"
alt="image005"
&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="http://blog.coinidea.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/09/image006.png"
loading="lazy"
alt="image006"
&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Install CDH&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="http://blog.coinidea.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/09/image007.png"
loading="lazy"
alt="image007"
&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Enter username and password&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="http://blog.coinidea.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/09/image008.png"
loading="lazy"
alt="image008"
&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="http://blog.coinidea.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/09/image009.png"
loading="lazy"
alt="image009"
&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="http://blog.coinidea.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/09/image010.png"
loading="lazy"
alt="image010"
&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Install the specified Parcel&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="http://blog.coinidea.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/09/image012.png"
loading="lazy"
alt="image012"
&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="http://blog.coinidea.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/09/image013.png"
loading="lazy"
alt="image013"
&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="http://blog.coinidea.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/09/image014.png"
loading="lazy"
alt="image014"
&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Select services&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="http://blog.coinidea.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/09/image015.png"
loading="lazy"
alt="image015"
&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;h1 id="4-storm"&gt;4. Storm
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;A distributed real-time computation system for processing high-speed, large-volume data streams. It adds reliable real-time data processing capabilities to Hadoop.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1 id="5-spark"&gt;5. Spark
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;Spark uses in-memory computing. Starting from multi-iteration batch processing, it allows data to be loaded into memory for repeated queries. It also integrates multiple computing paradigms such as data warehousing, stream processing, and graph computing. Spark is built on top of HDFS and integrates well with Hadoop.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1 id="6-problems"&gt;6. Problems
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Refreshing metadata packages&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;
&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-shell" data-lang="shell"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;Another app is currently holding the yum lock&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; waiting &lt;span class="k"&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; it to exit...
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;rm -f /var/run/yum.pid
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Uninstall Cloudera Manager&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;
&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-shell" data-lang="shell"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;$ sudo /usr/share/cmf/uninstall-cloudera-manager.sh
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Installation failed: Unable to receive heartbeat from Agent&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;
&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;3
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;4
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;5
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-shell" data-lang="shell"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;cat /etc/hosts
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;ip 域名 主机名
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;192.168.*.1 master.com master
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;cat /etc/sysconfig/network
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;HOSTNAME&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;master.com
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Uninstall Cloudera Manager&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;
&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt; 1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt; 2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt; 3
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt; 4
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt; 5
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt; 6
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt; 7
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt; 8
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt; 9
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;10
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;11
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;12
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;13
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;14
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;15
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
